# Picrew and Character Kit exports: 219MB of 600x600 PNGs, and the *input* to
# scripts/extract-picrew.ts rather than anything that ships. The build never
# reads this; `vite build` globs the derived art under
# src/client/avatar/sets/**/webp/, which is committed. Same bargain as .cache/
# above: the export is the source, the repo holds the derived copy, and a new
# drop of art is a rerun of extract:picrew. See sets/PROVENANCE.md for where
# these came from -- they are not re-downloadable on demand, so keep a copy.
CharacterCreator/
